# Overview

{{ project_slug }} is a modern Python template for machine learning projects. Built on PyTorch Lightning and uv{% if create_examples %}, it provides ML workflows for text, image, and tabular-data classification{% endif %}.

## Key Features

### 🚀 Modern Tool Stack
- **uv**: Fast Python package management and dependency resolution
- **PyTorch Lightning**: Scalable deep learning training workflows
- **{% if create_examples %}jsonargparse{% else %}Typer{% endif %}**: Intuitive CLI interface

{% if create_examples %}
### 🧠 Multi-Domain ML Support
- **NLP**: Semantic search with a frozen `BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5` embedding model (inference only)
- **Computer Vision**: CNN-based image classification (MNIST dataset)
- **Tabular Data**: Neural network-based tabular data classification (Titanic dataset)

{% endif %}
### 📁 Organized Project Structure
```
{{ project_slug }}/
├── src/{{ project_slug }}/     # Main source code
├── configs/                    # Configuration files (TOML)
├── data/                       # Data directories
│   ├── raw/                    # Original data
│   ├── processed/              # Processed data
│   ├── interim/                # Intermediate data
│   └── external/               # External data sources
├── docs/                       # Documentation
├── models/                     # Saved models
├── notebooks/                  # Jupyter notebooks
├── reports/                    # Generated reports
├── tests/                      # Tests
└── pyproject.toml              # Project configuration
```

## Supported Features

### CLI Commands
- `{{ project_slug }}-cli hello`: Smoke test command
{% if create_examples %}
- `{{ project_slug }}-cli nlp`: Semantic search over a small built-in corpus
- `{{ project_slug }}-cli tabular`: Train tabular data classification model
- `{{ project_slug }}-cli vision`: Train MNIST image classification model
{% endif %}

### Development Tools
- **Ruff**: Linting and formatting
- **ty**: Type checking
- **Pytest**: Unit testing
- **Pre-commit**: Code quality management
- **MkDocs**: Documentation generation

### Deployment Options
- **Docker**: Source code and package-based container images
- **PyPI**: Standard Python package distribution
- **Git-cliff**: Automated release note generation

## Architecture

### Model Training
- Modularized training pipeline based on PyTorch Lightning
- Automatic GPU/CPU detection and distributed training support
- TensorBoard logging and checkpoint management

### Code Quality
- Mandatory use of type hints (enforced by ty)
- Google-style docstrings
- Single quotes, 100-character line length coding conventions

